WEBVTT

00:12:55.450 --> 00:13:00.035
could become the same kind
of hub that we are,

00:13:00.059 --> 00:13:04.909
if the knowledge of how to do so
were present there.

00:13:05.758 --> 00:13:09.232
So, we're not in a uniquely
hospitable place.

00:13:09.256 --> 00:13:11.684
If intergalactic space
is capable of creating

00:13:11.708 --> 00:13:14.294
an open-ended stream of explanations,

00:13:14.318 --> 00:13:16.485
then so is almost every other environment,

00:13:16.509 --> 00:13:17.739
so is the Earth.

00:13:17.763 --> 00:13:20.093
So is a polluted Earth.

00:13:20.521 --> 00:13:24.268
And the limiting factor, there and here,

00:13:24.292 --> 00:13:27.066
is not resources --
because they're plentiful --

00:13:27.090 --> 00:13:29.240
but knowledge, which is scarce.

00:13:29.679 --> 00:13:35.580
Now, this cosmic knowledge-based view
may -- and, I think, ought to --